type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

! Views

A ''view'' is a tiddler that bundles a producer + arguments + overlay reference + engine preference. The `$mindmap` widget renders a view with `<$mindmap view="ViewTiddlerName"/>`.

!! View fields

|!Field |!Required |!Purpose |
|`mm.producer` |yes |Name of a registered `mindmap-producer` (e.g. `knowledge-tree`) |
|`mm.args` |yes |JSON object — arguments passed to the producer |
|`mm.overlay` |no |Title of the overlay tiddler holding the persistent op log |
|`mm.engine` |no |Engine name override; falls through to config default |
|`mm.options` |no |JSON object — engine-specific options |
|`mm.id-aliases` |no |JSON object mapping old ids to new ids (rename rescue) |

!! Existing views

<$list filter="[has[mm.producer]!is[system]sort[title]]" emptyMessage="No views defined yet.">
* <$link to=<<currentTiddler>>><<currentTiddler>></$link> — //producer:// {{!!mm.producer}}
</$list>

!! Creating a view

# Create a new tiddler (any title).
# Add field `mm.producer` with the name of an installed producer.
# Add field `mm.args` with a JSON object of arguments.
# Render with `<$mindmap view="..."/>` anywhere.

Example field values:

```
mm.producer:  knowledge-tree
mm.args:      {"area":"llm"}
mm.overlay:   $:/state/rimir/mindmap/views/my-map/overlay
mm.engine:    MindElixir
```
